/* FR-1.8.1 and FR-1.8.3: the log itself. The average is over the readings there are in the seven
   days ending on a given day, not over seven days each holding one — a lifter does not weigh in
   every morning, and the copy that says what would be enough is the average.none line below
   (FR-1.13.3).

   THE CARD AND A ROW NAME TWO DIFFERENT WINDOWS AND MUST NOT SHARE A LABEL. The card is the window
   ending TODAY; a row's caption is the window ending on that row's OWN day. They disagree whenever
   the last weigh-in is old — the card refuses while every row below it still carries a figure — so
   each says which window it means: "current" above, "to this date" on the row. */
"settings.bodyweight.title" = "Bodyweight";
"settings.bodyweight.add.action" = "Add reading";
"settings.bodyweight.average.title" = "Current seven-day average";
"settings.bodyweight.average.none" = "Weigh in twice within seven days to see your current average.";
